RetroBoot a72dvfs: A72 (cpu8/9) DVFS above 1495 MHz on the Gemini PDA (MT6797X)

Applied by build-kernel.sh --variant a72dvfs, after patches/*.patch, on top of
gemini-nixos 6a172f5's kernel delta (GPL-2.0). Upstream's plan steps a72dvfs2/3
(docs/cpu-dvfs.md); vendor reference gemian/gemini-linux-kernel-3.18
drivers/misc/mediatek/base/power/mt6797/{mt_cpufreq.c,mt_idvfs.c} @ 8cfe659.

- regulator: mt6797-sramldo-b, the A72 SRAM LDO (VSRAM_B):
  - set: SiP SMC 0xC20003BF with mV x 100, grid values only (vosel 3..15 = 0.9..1.2 V
    in 25 mV steps); hard limits 1.0..1.2 V;
  - readback: the vendor way (secure read 0x102222b0 while an A72 is online);
  - not used: the GET SMC 0xC20003C0, which the vendor never calls.
- mediatek-cpufreq (MT6797):
  - never enables or disables the cluster rails; sets a voltage only while the proc
    rail is on;
  - speed bin from LK's devinfo (nvmem cells) selects opp-supported-hw;
  - mediatek,intermediate-microvolt floor (vendor lifts VPROC2 to OPP9 = 1.0 V
    while on MAINPLL);
  - retroboot,boot-max-frequency-khz boot cap, moved into scaling_max_freq at
    ->ready().
- DTS:
  - cpu8 proc/sram supplies and properties; VPROC2 ramp delay; the VSRAM_B node;
  - devinfo cells;
  - bin-gated A72 OPP table (SB 0119 + TT; <= 1495 MHz kept at the proven 1.000 V);
  - an 80 C passive trip for the A72s only (the 85 C trip is unchanged).
